The carcinogenic risk of the studied heavy metals in carrots and cucumbers was assessed
by calculating the Excess Lifetime Cancer Risk (ELCR) using Eq. 4 [39]. In Eq. 4 CSF is
the cancer slope factor. CSF for Pb, Cd, Cr, and Ni is 6.3, 0.0085, 0.5, 0.91, respectively

