1.5 Significance of the study
The research is important in the following aspects:
Scientific Significance
i.
Provides all-inclusive soil-crop contamination
information in Niger state.
ii. Improves the knowledge on soil-to-plant transfer
in the tropical agricultural systems.
iii. Favors the modeling and contamination-pathway
studies of the environment.
Public-Health Significance
I.
Brings evidence to early detection and prevention
of risks of dietary exposure.\
II. Helps determine the vulnerable populations that
are in need of much-needed health intervention.
Policy and Social Economic Significance.
i.
Provides scientific evidence on environmental
control and management of agricultural-input.
ii. Helps in food-safety surveillance, pollutionreduction measures and also sustainable land
management.
1.6 Scope of the study
This study focuses on:
Chosen Local Government Areas in the state of Niger
such as Bida, Lapai, Mokwa, Shiroro, Munya, Rafi,
and Paikoro.
I.
Soil and crop sampling of contaminants.
II. Evaluation of heavy metal and other vital
contaminants.
